  "title": "OpenBMI SSVEP EEG dataset (Lee et al. 2019)",
  "description": "A BIDS-formatted derivative of the OpenBMI SSVEP EEG dataset (Lee et al., 2019), organized via the Mother of All BCI Benchmarks (MOABB) framework. It contains 62-channel EEG recorded at 1000 Hz from 54 subjects across two sessions, with four-class steady-state visually evoked potential stimulation (21,600 trials of 4 s each). The dataset supports standardized benchmarking of SSVEP-based brain-computer interface methods.",
  "methods_description": "Original OpenBMI recordings were converted to BIDS using MNE-BIDS via the MOABB pipeline. Data comprise 62 EEG channels sampled at 1000 Hz, with 4-second SSVEP trials in 4 classes across 2 sessions per subject.",
